This lists known issue with dependencies and such.

Libfaketime 0.99.7 has a bug that can cause segfaults during testbench
runs. If you experience them, either use --disable-libfaketime configure
switch or go back to an older version.
see also: https://github.com/rsyslog/rsyslog/issues/2099

On Solaris 11 x64 (SunStudio build), tests/segmented-da-tcp-spill-exact.sh
fails: tcpflood reports "CLOSED REMOTELY (Broken pipe)" after about 64
messages per connection while imtcp feeds a segmented disk-assisted main
queue under backpressure. It is skipped on SunOS. The root cause is not yet
known; remove the skip once it is fixed.
see also: https://github.com/rsyslog/rsyslog/issues/7917

On Solaris 11 x64 (SunStudio build), tests/imrelp-tls-chainedcert.sh and
tests/imrelp-tls-mixed-chainedcert.sh fail: imrelp with tls.authmode="certvalid"
rejects the client certificate file that contains a chain ("certificate verify
failed" in the server handshake), while the unchained imrelp TLS tests pass.
They are skipped on SunOS. The root cause (librelp/OpenSSL version on the
builder) has not been analysed; remove the skips once it is understood.
